#pragma once

// World Dungeon "System Carl" theme -- companion species set.
// Generated by Pixel, 2026-08-19. Phase 4 follow-up to
// world_dungeon_system_carl_sprites.h, per Forge's species pool (msg 386,
// HEAD 9d5a91d on phase-7-world-dungeon-correctness) and parent's greenlight
// (msg 388).
//
// Same convention as the base set: 14x20, stride 2, levels 0/3 only (LSB == MSB
// == "is this pixel blank" mask). Ink density held in the 20-35% band per parent's
// instruction -- companions read as small/distinguishable, not threats, and the
// same silhouette-collapse risk applies above ~40%. Outline family (legged vs
// floating, curved vs angular) is the primary differentiator between species --
// see per-function comments in gen.py, especially Shadow Sprite vs Grid Sprite,
// which share a name suffix and are deliberately built from opposite silhouette
// families (smooth taper vs stepped right angles) so they don't get confused.
//
// Note: no local #include for Sprite2bpp.h here -- GameTheme.h already
// includes it before including this file (same convention as
// world_dungeon_system_carl_sprites.h). A local prefixed include broke the
// host gtest build (dirty_rect_planner's include dir is src/game only, not
// repo root, so "game/Sprite2bpp.h" didn't resolve there even though it did
// under PlatformIO's broader embedded-build include search).

